  <h1>Java Variables</h1>

  <p>Variables are containers for storing data values. In Java, each variable must be declared with a data type.</p>

  <p><strong>Types of Variables:</strong></p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Local Variable</strong> - defined inside a method or block</li>
    <li><strong>Instance Variable</strong> - defined in a class, outside any method</li>
    <li><strong>Static Variable</strong> - declared with the <code>static</code> keyword</li>
  </ul>

  <p><strong>Simple Java Code:</strong></p>
  <pre><code>
public class Variables {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int age = 30;
        String name = "Alice";
        double salary = 45678.90;

        System.out.println("Name: " + name);
        System.out.println("Age: " + age);
        System.out.println("Salary: $" + salary);
    }
}
  </code></pre>

